  "description": "<p>Per <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" data-account-id=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" accountid=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Aaron Birkland</a>, \"it looks like fcrepo-http-commons and fcrepo-kernel-modeshape both pull in a JTA dependency: org.jboss.jbossts:jbossjta</p>\n\n<p>\"However, it looks really old and unmaintained – the latest release is five years old: <a href=\"https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.jboss.jbossts/jbossjta\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.jboss.jbossts/jbossjta</a>\"</p>\n\n<p>We should update to Modeshape's new recommended JTA, Narayana. The latest version is 5.7.0.Final.</p>\n",
